questions.corrige_markdown:
Draw a smooth fixed pulley with the light string passing over it, M (4 kg) hanging on one side and N (5 kg) on the other. The forces are:

- on M: the weight $4g=40$ N acting **downwards** and the tension $T$ acting **upwards** along the string;
- on N: the weight $5g=50$ N acting **downwards** and the same tension $T$ acting **upwards** along the string (the pulley is smooth and the string light, so the tension is the same on both sides);
- on the pulley: its support force (the fixed support pulls up with $2T$).

Also mark the direction of motion: N (the heavier mass) moves down and M moves up, with the same acceleration $a$.
